# Kirchhoff's current law, read off three ammeters.
#
# A 9 V battery feeds two resistors side by side. Each resistor has an ammeter in series with it, and
# a third ammeter sits in the battery's own lead, so it reads what both take together.
#
# Ohm's law gives each branch: 9 V across R1 (1 kΩ) is 9 mA, and across R2 (500 Ω) is 18 mA. The
# current into the junction equals the current out of it, so the total is the sum: A3 reads 27 mA.
#
# An ammeter reads positive when current flows in at the end it was drawn from.

battery  B1   0 0  0 8  9V
ammeter  A3   0 0  6 0
wire          6 0  12 0
wire          12 0  22 0

ammeter  A1   12 0  12 4
resistor R1   12 4  12 8  1k

ammeter  A2   22 0  22 4
resistor R2   22 4  22 8  500

wire          0 8  12 8
wire          12 8  22 8
ground        0 8
